{% doc %}
  Routes page types to the structured-data snippets that apply to them.

  Rendered once from `layout/theme.liquid`, in the head, immediately after
  `meta-tags`. Deliberately NOT rendered from `layout/password.liquid`: the
  password page is not the storefront and should not carry entity markup.

  Today this emits Organization and WebSite, and only on the homepage, so the
  store has exactly one of each rather than one per page.

  Not everything routes through here. `sections/faq.liquid` emits its own
  `FAQPage` node, and `snippets/breadcrumbs.liquid` emits its own `BreadcrumbList`
  node, because in both cases the markup is derived from the same data as the
  visible markup beside it and has no meaning away from it. Keeping the
  `BreadcrumbList` in the breadcrumb snippet is what guarantees the trail and the
  structured data cannot disagree. Page-scoped markup belongs with the thing it
  describes; this router is for site-wide entity nodes.

  Product and ProductGroup markup is not routed here. It comes from Shopify's
  `{{ product | structured_data }}` filter in `sections/product-information.liquid`
  and the featured-product sections, which is Shopify-maintained and not
  extensible.

  @example
    {%- render 'structured-data' -%}
{% enddoc %}

{%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
  {%- render 'structured-data-organization' -%}
  {%- render 'structured-data-website' -%}
{%- endif -%}
